      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0009:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0009",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "For example, consider the effects of different [`particleColorVariation`](scnparticlesystem/particlecolorvariation.md) vectors on a system whose [`particleColor`](scnparticlesystem/particlecolor.md) property specifies a fully opaque red as the base color:",
      "normalizedSource": "For example, consider the effects of different [`particleColorVariation`](scnparticlesystem/particlecolorvariation.md) vectors on a system whose [`particleColor`](scnparticlesystem/particlecolor.md) property specifies a fully opaque red as the base color:",
      "sourceHash": "250b6d45cd6b733a0225bf9b9adb03de9c4e9373e704363bc981dd9daa048fd4",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "The components of the vector specify ranges of variation in hue, saturation, brightness, and alpha, in that order.",
      "contextAfter": "The vector `{0.25, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0}` allows newly spawned particles to take on any hue within a quarter of the color wheel centered on red (that is, ranging from purple through magenta, red, orange, and yellow to green). Particles retain full saturation, brightness, and alpha.",
      "documentTitle": "particleColorVariation",
      "framework": "SceneKit",
