      "type": "list_item",
      "source": "The vector `{0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0}` allows newly spawned particles to vary in alpha between full and half opacity. (The range of variation is centered on the base value, but clamped to a maximum of `1.0`.) Particles retain the same hue, saturation, and brightness as the base color.",
      "normalizedSource": "The vector `{0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0}` allows newly spawned particles to vary in alpha between full and half opacity. (The range of variation is centered on the base value, but clamped to a maximum of `1.0`.) Particles retain the same hue, saturation, and brightness as the base color.",
      "sourceHash": "3a8f46249357a513cc3b7513afa36a5d85608c191924afb49be6aa8b3953f2f6",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "The vector `{0.25, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0}` allows newly spawned particles to take on any hue within a quarter of the color wheel centered on red (that is, ranging from purple through magenta, red, orange, and yellow to green). Particles retain full saturation, brightness, and alpha.",
      "contextAfter": "The vector `{0.0, 1.0, 1.0, 0.0}` allows newly spawned particles to vary in saturation and brightness, resulting in random shades of red. Particles retain the same hue and alpha as the base color.",
